    "text": "Pakistan invites Turkmenistan to join CASA-1000! ⚡\nAccording to Business Recorder, Federal Minister for Energy (Power Division) Sardar Awais Ahmad Khan Leghari invited Turkmenistan to join the CASA-1000 electricity transmission project during a meeting in Islamabad with Turkmenistan's Minister of Energy Annageldi Saparov. Leghari also proposed making the line two-way, so countries can exchange power when needed. Saparov reaffirmed Turkmenistan's commitment to the TAP power project, which he said could serve over 300 million people.\nCan regional power links help Pakistan? Tell us in the comments 👇\n\nImage: AI-generated illustration.\n\n#RiseUpPakistan #CASA1000 #Turkmenistan #Energy #PakistanNews",
